From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:20:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wlrandr: Do not start under Caminito

The plugin keeps the display layout in monitors-wayland.xml and applies it
over wlr-output-management when the session starts. Caminito, the Wayland
compositor for MATE, keeps the layouts itself, one for each set of
connected monitors, and restores them before its first frame. With both,
the plugin would apply its own layout over the one Caminito restored.

When MATE_WM_NAME is Caminito, do not start the manager. Without that
variable, nothing changes.
---
 plugins/wlrandr/msd-wlrandr-plugin.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plugins/wlrandr/msd-wlrandr-plugin.c b/plugins/wlrandr/msd-wlrandr-plugin.c
index 522e122..01d763f 100644
--- a/plugins/wlrandr/msd-wlrandr-plugin.c
+++ b/plugins/wlrandr/msd-wlrandr-plugin.c
@@ -70,6 +70,14 @@ impl_activate (MateSettingsPlugin *plugin)
         gboolean res;
         GError  *error;
 
+        /* Caminito, the Wayland compositor for MATE, saves and restores the
+         * display layouts itself, and this plugin's layout would be applied
+         * over the one it restored. */
+        if (g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("MATE_WM_NAME"), "Caminito") == 0) {
+                g_debug ("Not activating wlrandr plugin under Caminito");
+                return;
+        }
+
         g_debug ("Activating wlrandr plugin");
 
         error = NULL;
